jobs.description:
Location: Toronto, Canada
Reports to: Founder & CEO

About Leon Cycle

Leon Cycle was founded in Germany in 2014 and has since expanded across Europe, North America and Australia.

We design, manufacture and sell electric bicycles through dealer networks, key accounts and e-commerce channels. Our flagship brand, NCM, offers a wide range of e-bikes across trekking, city, mountain and folding categories.

We are now looking for a Sales & Operations Director Canada to lead the next stage of growth of our Canada business.

The Role

You will take overall responsibility for the sales, operations and P&L performance of Leon Cycle Canada.

This is not a pure sales role. You will lead both commercial growth and local operations, ensuring strong execution across sales, inventory, logistics, customer service and after-sales.

Key Responsibilities

* Develop and execute the Canadian sales and growth strategy;
* Recruit, lead and coach 3 Business Development Managers;
* Expand our dealer network and develop Key Accounts;
* Own Canadian revenue, gross margin and P&L performance;
* Manage the sales pipeline, pricing and commercial performance;
* Directly manage the Canadian Operations Manager;
* Oversee inventory, 3PL, warehouse, logistics and delivery performance;
* Oversee customer service, returns, warranty and technical support;
* Oversee the Leon Cycle Ride & Service Hub – Toronto;
* Work closely with shared Finance, HR, Marketing and E-commerce teams;
* Identify and resolve operational and commercial issues quickly.

Initial Team Structure

Sales & Operations Director – Canada

* Business Development Managers × 3
* Operations Manager
* Warehouse & Logistics
* Customer Service
* Technical Support
* Technician / Mechanic

What We’re Looking For

* 10+ years of commercial, sales or business management experience;
* Proven experience leading B2B sales and dealer/channel development;
* Strong Key Account and negotiation experience;
* Experience managing both sales and operations;
* Good understanding of P&L, gross margin, inventory and working capital;
* Experience with 3PL, logistics, customer service or after-sales operations;
* Experience in e-bikes, bicycles, automotive, motorcycles, consumer electronics or durable consumer goods is preferred;
* Entrepreneurial, hands-on, data-driven and highly accountable;
* Strong leadership and communication skills.

What Success Looks Like

Build a profitable, scalable and high-performing Canadian business with strong sales growth, an expanding dealer network, healthy inventory and reliable customer service.

This role is ideal for a commercially driven leader who wants to build and own a business, rather than simply manage a sales team.

Show more

Show less

Seniority level

Director

Employment type

Full-time

Industries

Sporting Goods Manufacturing and Electrical Equipment Manufacturing

